# Performance & Security Hardening (Permanent)

## HTTP surface

- **CORS:** allow only `CORS_ORIGINS` (comma list); credentials on; no `*`.
- **Helmet:** enabled on Nest HTTP (secure headers). Do not disable in production for convenience.
- **Trust proxy:** when `TRUST_PROXY=true`, enable Express trust proxy so IP allowlists / rate keys see real client IPs behind reverse proxies.
- **Next.js same-origin redirects behind a proxy:** middleware redirects for locale/auth navigation must use an absolute URL built from the validated public origin, so internal container hosts and ports never reach the browser. Next middleware requires an absolute redirect URL. Trust forwarded host/protocol headers only when Nginx sets them from the ingress request; do not trust arbitrary client-supplied values.
- **Dependency health diagnostics:** public health responses expose status only; logs may include sanitized dependency error names/codes and non-secret target host/port/database, but never full connection URLs, credentials, or raw error messages. Unwrap nested causes and classify only allowlisted error codes/signatures; suppress duplicate warnings until the failure changes or recovers.

## Rate limits (Redis)

| Surface | Keys / knobs |
| --- | --- |
| OTP | existing `OTP_*` |
| Share unlock | existing `SHARE_LINK_*` |
| PDF **final** export enqueue | `EXPORT_RATE_MAX` / `EXPORT_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS` per `businessId` |
| PDF **preview** enqueue (ADR 036) | `EXPORT_PREVIEW_RATE_MAX` / `EXPORT_PREVIEW_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS`; in-flight `EXPORT_PREVIEW_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_BUSINESS` |

## Export queue cost controls

- Cap **in-flight** **final** jobs per Business: `queued` + `processing` with purpose final ≤ `EXPORT_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_BUSINESS`.
- Cap **in-flight preview** jobs separately: ≤ `EXPORT_PREVIEW_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_BUSINESS` (default 1) — previews must not starve finals (ADR 036).
- Worker concurrency: `EXPORT_WORKER_CONCURRENCY` (default 1 — PDF is CPU/RAM heavy).
- Never run PDF render on the interactive HTTP path (editor keystroke / autosave / DnD).

## Data / indexes

- Every tenant table queried by `businessId` must keep a supporting index (usually `(businessId, …)`).
- List APIs stay paginated; no unbounded tenant scans.

## IDOR

- Path `:businessId` + membership on every tenant read/write; Mongo filters always include `businessId`.

## Forbidden

- Opening CORS to `*` with credentials.
- Unbounded concurrent PDF jobs per tenant.
- Skipping Helmet in SAAS/SELF_HOSTED production images without an ADR.
